From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carlos Duran <15650777+carlos-duran@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] BananaDS: Auto keeps a session others are in when the game's
 wifi goes off

M ended an Auto session once the game's wifi had been off for 3 s, to go
back to waiting when the game leaves its multiplayer mode. Mario Kart DS
keeps its wifi off for longer than that between looking for groups and
creating one: an Auto host with a desktop melonDS player in its session
ended it there and hosted a new one, while the player's melonDS kept the
old session (its lobby showed the host as "Connection lost") and its game
found no group.

The 3 s rule now applies only to a host alone in its session. With others
in it (Auto hosting them, or joined to a host), the session stays while
the game's wifi is off, as Host's and Join's do and as in L. Disconnect,
a lost host and a lost network still end it.
---
 bananads/docs/SETTINGS.md |  2 +-
 bananads/src/emu.cpp      | 18 +++++++++---------
 bananads/src/emu.h        |  2 +-
 3 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bananads/docs/SETTINGS.md b/bananads/docs/SETTINGS.md
index c724494..f2433c9 100644
--- a/bananads/docs/SETTINGS.md
+++ b/bananads/docs/SETTINGS.md
@@ -78,7 +78,7 @@ key can also come from the environment as `BANANADS_<KEY>` (dots become undersco
 | `firmware.language` | the firmware's | 0 Japanese, 1 English, 2 French, 3 German, 4 Italian, 5 Spanish |
 | `rtc.fixed` | none | the DS clock's start, `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS` (or `T` or `_` for the space), instead of the current time: two runs of a game that seeds its random numbers from the clock then go the same way (for tests) |
 | `wifi.dns` | `kaeru` | `kaeru`, `altwfc`, `wiilink`, an IPv4 address, `system` (the handheld's own DNS) or `off` (no Wi-Fi at all) |
-| `wifi.local` | `off` | local wireless with other handhelds or desktop melonDS on the same network (builds with `BANANADS_LAN`): `host` (a session others join), `join` (look for hosts; pick one in the in-game menu's LAN multiplayer page), `join:<the host's address>` (join that host at the start) or `auto` (see below). The menu's page changes it while the game runs and keeps `off`, `auto`, `host` or `join` here for the next game (a join keeps `join`, not the address).<br>`auto`: nothing until the game turns its wifi on (its multiplayer menu, Download Play); then it listens for the hosts' beacons for 2-3 s and joins a host of the same game (melonDS patch 0096's tag: one hosting by hand first, else the lowest address), else a host that doesn't say its game (desktop melonDS) if no tagged one is there, else hosts. Of two that start together and both host, the one alone with the higher address joins the other once it has heard it twice. Nothing changes during a local wireless game; a player whose host leaves looks again (one of those left hosts); a game that goes online through Nintendo WFC gets no session. When the game turns its wifi off for 3 s of its own time (it left its multiplayer mode; MKDS turns it off and on for under 2 s between its screens), Auto ends or leaves its session and waits again (the others look again); the paused menu doesn't count. Every console in the room on `auto` (or one on `host`, the others on `auto`) is enough.<br>No network (no interface other than loopback up, connected and with an IPv4 address; checked every 1 s): nothing starts and no join is tried, the mode stays as chosen (here too); a session ends when the network goes (the others look again); when it is back, `host` hosts again, `join` looks for hosts, `auto` starts over once the game's wifi is on. Nintendo WFC (slirp) isn't affected |
+| `wifi.local` | `off` | local wireless with other handhelds or desktop melonDS on the same network (builds with `BANANADS_LAN`): `host` (a session others join), `join` (look for hosts; pick one in the in-game menu's LAN multiplayer page), `join:<the host's address>` (join that host at the start) or `auto` (see below). The menu's page changes it while the game runs and keeps `off`, `auto`, `host` or `join` here for the next game (a join keeps `join`, not the address).<br>`auto`: nothing until the game turns its wifi on (its multiplayer menu, Download Play); then it listens for the hosts' beacons for 2-3 s and joins a host of the same game (melonDS patch 0096's tag: one hosting by hand first, else the lowest address), else a host that doesn't say its game (desktop melonDS) if no tagged one is there, else hosts. Of two that start together and both host, the one alone with the higher address joins the other once it has heard it twice. Nothing changes during a local wireless game; a player whose host leaves looks again (one of those left hosts); a game that goes online through Nintendo WFC gets no session. When the game turns its wifi off for 3 s of its own time (it left its multiplayer mode; MKDS turns it off and on for under 2 s between its screens) while Auto hosts a session nobody else is in, the session ends and Auto waits again; the paused menu doesn't count. With others in the session (Auto hosting them, or in a host's session) it stays, as `host`'s and `join`'s do: MKDS keeps its wifi off for longer than 3 s between looking for groups and creating one. Every console in the room on `auto` (or one on `host`, the others on `auto`) is enough.<br>No network (no interface other than loopback up, connected and with an IPv4 address; checked every 1 s): nothing starts and no join is tried, the mode stays as chosen (here too); a session ends when the network goes (the others look again); when it is back, `host` hosts again, `join` looks for hosts, `auto` starts over once the game's wifi is on. Nintendo WFC (slirp) isn't affected |
 | `wifi.local_players` | `4` | `host`, `auto`: how many may be in the session, the host included (2-16) |
 | `wifi.local_auto_start` | `wifi` | `auto`: `wifi` waits for the game to turn its wifi on; `now` starts at once (for tests with a game that doesn't) |
 | `wifi.local_auto_test_wifi` | (none) | `auto`, for tests: the game's wifi as a script by frame, e.g. `on@0,off@2400,on@2500` (instead of the DS's own) |
diff --git a/bananads/src/emu.cpp b/bananads/src/emu.cpp
index 651cb9e..1929871 100644
--- a/bananads/src/emu.cpp
+++ b/bananads/src/emu.cpp
@@ -583,10 +583,16 @@ void Emu::lan_auto_tick() {
     // the game's wifi off for 3 s of its own time (frames run: the paused menu doesn't count): it has left its
     // multiplayer mode, so it isn't in a local wireless game. MKDS turns it off and on again between its own
     // screens and races, for under 2 s.
+    // Only a host alone in its session ends it so: with others in it (a host's players, or a joined player's host),
+    // the session stays, as Host's and Join's do. MKDS keeps its wifi off for longer than that between looking for
+    // groups and creating one, and the others' melonDS would keep a session that had ended.
     const bool wifi_gone = auto_wifi_off_frames_ >= kAutoWifiGrace;
+    const bool alone = auto_phase_ == AutoPhase::Host && static_cast<LAN&>(MPInterface::Get()).GetNumPlayers() <= 1;
     if (wifi != auto_wifi_was_ && (auto_phase_ == AutoPhase::Host || auto_phase_ == AutoPhase::Joined))
         Log(LogLevel::Info, "[wifi] local wireless auto: the game's wifi %s\n",
-            wifi ? "is on again: the session stays" : "went off: the session ends if it stays off for 3 s");
+            wifi ? "is on again: the session stays"
+            : alone ? "went off: the session ends if it stays off for 3 s while nobody else is in it"
+                    : "went off: the session stays (others are in it)");
     auto_wifi_was_ = wifi;
     auto_bad_.erase(std::remove_if(auto_bad_.begin(), auto_bad_.end(),
                                    [t](const std::pair<uint32_t, uint64_t>& b) { return b.second <= t; }),
@@ -645,7 +651,7 @@ void Emu::lan_auto_tick() {
         }
         case AutoPhase::Host: {
             LAN& lan = static_cast<LAN&>(MPInterface::Get());
-            if (wifi_gone) {  // (the others, if any, look again)
+            if (wifi_gone && alone) {
                 lan_stop();
                 Log(LogLevel::Info, "[wifi] local wireless auto: the game turned its wifi off: the session ends, waiting\n");
                 lan_auto_phase(AutoPhase::Wait, "The game turned its wireless off: the session ended");
@@ -691,13 +697,7 @@ void Emu::lan_auto_tick() {
             }
             break;
         }
-        case AutoPhase::Joined:  // (a lost host: lan_refresh)
-            if (wifi_gone) {
-                lan_stop();
-                Log(LogLevel::Info, "[wifi] local wireless auto: the game turned its wifi off: we leave the session, waiting\n");
-                lan_auto_phase(AutoPhase::Wait, "The game turned its wireless off: we left the session");
-                break;
-            }
+        case AutoPhase::Joined:  // (a lost host: lan_refresh; the game's wifi off: we stay, see above)
             if (wfc && !mp_active()) {  // joined while the game looked for an access point: it went online
                 lan_stop();
                 Log(LogLevel::Info, "[wifi] local wireless auto: the game is online (Nintendo WFC): we leave the session\n");
diff --git a/bananads/src/emu.h b/bananads/src/emu.h
index 33488fa..a2f7a94 100644
--- a/bananads/src/emu.h
+++ b/bananads/src/emu.h
@@ -196,7 +196,7 @@ private:
     uint64_t net_check_us_ = 0;
     long auto_wifi_off_frames_ = 0;           // frames run in a row with the game's wifi off
     bool auto_wifi_was_ = false;              // (the log: the game's wifi off and on within a session)
-    static constexpr long kAutoWifiGrace = 180;  // 3 s of the game's time: a wifi off that long ends Auto's session
+    static constexpr long kAutoWifiGrace = 180;  // 3 s of the game's time: a wifi off that long ends an Auto host's session with nobody else in it
     AutoPhase auto_phase_ = AutoPhase::Wait;
     uint64_t auto_tick_us_ = 0, auto_deadline_us_ = 0, auto_host_since_us_ = 0;
     uint32_t auto_my_ip_ = 0;                 // our address, from our own beacon (0: not heard yet)
